# "You may sacrifice another creature" is one creature, not two (refused: Memnite and Ornithopter together), and the counters are the
# sacrificed creature's power: Bot1 sacrifices its Memnite, power 1, and the Rampager gets one counter - a 4/3 - and hits Bot2 for 4 (16).
# The Ornithopter (power 0) stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mana Crypt
Memnite
Ornithopter
Rhovanion Rampager
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mana Crypt.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mana Crypt.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rhovanion Rampager.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Rhovanion Rampager > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Choose(Memnite; Ornithopter)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Rhovanion Rampager.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Rhovanion Rampager.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Rhovanion Rampager.Toughness = 3
Bot2.Life = 16
